    "1. Outline  1) Microorganisms that oxidize and decompose odor materials and VOCs form bioflims in media that are filled in the reactor.  2) The odor materials and VOCs that are transported to BIO-CAT are adsorbed and absorbed on the surfaces of biofilms. The microorganisms decompose. by oxidation reactions. them into CO2. H2O. and materials that are harmless to human body.    2. Advantages  1) Possible to simultaneously treat odor and VOCs  2) Fast discomposing and minimization of pressure loss  3) Strong durability and low cost of maintenance  4) Maximization of removal efficiency by selecting microorganisms according to odor and VOCs materials  5) Fully automatic operation method    3. Application fields  1) Sewerage. wastewater. and night soil treatment facilities  2) Food waste treatment facilities  3) Fish and meat processing factories  4) Painting and ink processes of automobiles and electronic products  5) Manufacturing processes of solvents. adherents. and synthetic fibers  6) Plastic manufacturing processes  7) Other odor and VOCs generating sites": 1,
    "1. Outline  The unit sterilizes E. Coli and other germs in water. using UV lamp that emits rays of 230 ~ 270 nm.    2. Introduction  Generation of fine vibration in the inflow water increases the possibility that UV rays contact germs. thereby maximizing sterilization. In particular. pulse vibrator (patented) is used to maximize sterilization(See Fig1).     3. Characteristics  1) Easy maintenance  - Easy to maintain: Possible to separate and substitute lamp by opening the top cover only.  - Prevent the attachment of foreign materials to quartz sleeves of UV lamp and the formation of scale.  2) Contacting tank of flowing and floating  - The plate to lead water flow is of the S character shape. which increases the opportunity for germs to contact UV rays. Thus the sterilization opportunity is increased.   3) The unit can be installed in any places.  - The installation area is half of the horizontal type and can be easily installed even in the prior contacting tanks of chlorine sterilization.  -Possible to install in the prior chlorine sterilization tanks. at proper locations such as undergrounds. roofs. machine rooms. etc.   - Low operation cost: one bank is manufactured and installed in many modules. Thus depending on the load. proper modules only are operated. thus saving the operation cost greatly.    4. Application  Sterilization of supply water and sewerage": 1,
    "1. Outline   The facility is an integrated dust collector that has a bagfilter at the top portion ad a cyclone at the bottom.    2. Introduction  1) Performance of Cybagfilter   We developed a cyclone shape of high efficiency by computational analysis using CFD(Computational Fluid Dynamic). Cybagfilter collects 70% of dusts with sub-micron (less than 1 mm) and 95% of dusts with more than 10 mm at the cyclone part.    2) De-dusting system of bagfilter in Cybagfilter  - Air line pulse jet is used for de-dusting.  - Our company developed various types of air line spray nozzles to improve the de-dusting function. which are most optimal for de-dusting systems.    3. Characteristics  1) The structure is simple and it is possible to install them in a limited space.   2) The dust load in filtration cloth is reduced.   3) It is possible to extend the de-dusting interval  4) We possess the design technology of Compact Hybrid Dust Collector  5) The operation. maintenance. and installation costs are reduced compared to the prior dust collectors.   6) The life time of filtration clothes are extended by more than twice    4. Application  1) Factories to install dust collectors   2) Factories to reorganize or substitute superannuated dust collectors  3) Factories with small installation areas for dust collectors   4) Industries with dusts difficult to collect or de-dust.   5) Factories with the measures for controlling the total volume of contaminants.": 1,
    "1. Outline  EB-Deduster is a dust collector that adopts the advantages of electric dust collection and bag filtering. EB-Deduster is developed to maintain the dust collection efficiency by using the advantages and to reduce the operation cost.    2. Introduction  In the entrance of EB-Deduster. a corona discharging area is installed for dusts to be charged with negative charges. The charged particles are collected on the surface of filtration clothes by electrostatic attraction. The density reduction of the dust layer formed there reduces the pressure loss. Thus. the density reduction increases the dust collection efficiency of fine dusts with less than 1 mm.    3. Characteristics  1) The remnant pressure loss is reduced by 30%   2) The de-dusting interval is extended by more than twice   3) The life time of filtration cloths is extended by more than twice.   4) It is possible to save the energy consumption by about 15%.   5) The dust collection efficiency of fine dust particles is improved by about 5%   6) It is possible to maintain the total dust collection efficiency at more than 99.9%     4. Application  1) Factories to install dust collectors   2) Factories to reorganize or substitute superannuated dust collectors  3) Factories with small installation areas for dust collectors   4) Industries with dusts difficult to collect or de-dust.   5) Factories with the measures for controlling the total volume of contaminants.": 1,
    "1. Outline  Restoration of contaminated soil using microorganisms treat contaminated soil biologically without incinerating the soil contaminated with oil or bringing soil from other places.    2. Introduction  Biological decomposition processes of contaminated soil using microorganisms     3. Characteristics  1) Restoration using microorganisms allow in-situ treatment. Thus wide contaminated areas can be treated economically and effectively.  2) The soil restoration period can be minimized.  3) Biological reaction by microorganisms is continuous and accelerated. Thus. when this method is used repeatedly. the treatment speed is increased and the secondary contamination can be prevented.  4) Since restoration can occur as the underground water flows. there is the effect of additional restoration.    4. Application   Oil-contaminated soil": 1,
    "1. Outline  The apparatus uses waste glasses or various glasses that are mixed with other materials to make round-edged glass powder or chips using several processes.(See Fig.1)      2. Introduction  Metals. plastics. and papers are removed without manual works (the size range is 1 to 10 mm). The particles that are went through the processes are used for glassphalt. filtration. drainage. Abrasives. landscaping. etc.    3. Characteristics  1) Flexible impact mechanism  - Prevent wear and abrasion of the part related to the grinder (patented technology)  2) Heavy duty bearing  - They are isolated from other parts and closed in a case. The wearing parts can be easily substituted.  3) Each of glass pulverizer. two conveyors. and trommel separator includes metering surge hopper.  4) Pulverization system of high shock  - Different from other facilities. this system makes other grinding processes unnecessary. Also since the system generates round-edged glass particles. it is easy to apply the final products for various purposes.    4. Application  Waste glasses are reutilized for asphalt. materials for roads after mixing with cement. materials for preventing erosion of coasts. materials for soil. backfill materials for highways. etc.": 1,
    "1. Outline  PVC dual pipe having a rubber ring inserted into a pipe.  This product is used for public sewage pipes or sewage and rainwater pipes for apartment. etc.    2. Introduction(See Figure)      3. Characteristics  1) Good strength: Have the highest pipe stiffness as a ductility sewage pipe (over 8kgf/cm² in case of PVC dual wall pipe 5% change on the basis of KS)  2) Good constructability  3) Good water tightness: Guarantee water tightness with a rubber ring joint.  4) Suitable for environmental protection: Prevent introduction of underground water and contamination of soil.  Can be recycled as pure plastic products.  5) Chemical-resistant: Resistant to various chemicals such as acid. alkali. etc.. impossible bacteria inhabitation.  6) Creep properties: PVC dual wall pipe is very low in the creep property compared to HDPE.  Thus. PVC dual wall pipe has almost no transformation even after a long time. but HDPE is weak in a long-tern weight and is easily transformed.  7) Rubber ring: EPDM material of good physical properties and semi-permanent.  8) Auto-digestion    4. Applications  1) Sewage and rainwater tributary pipes for public sewage  2) Sewage and rainwater main pipes for apartments  3) Intercepting pipe line for sewage treatment": 1,
    "Water treatment apparatus through advanced oxidization process &amp;#8211; using ozone and ultraviolet    1. Outline  The apparatus removes difficult-to-decompose contaminants in water by oxidative decomposition by using intermediate products called the OH radical that are formed by the reaction of ozone with UV. The present apparatus performs water purification while floating on the surface of the storage tank. and forms a water purification unit integrally with the ozone filter.    2. Introduction  TANK MAN&amp;reg; is an apparatus for enhancing an inefficient production power of OH radicals that are generated by an existing AOP in which air is blown in a minute bubble state from the bottom in a state where an ultraviolet rays lamp is simply put into a water tank. Fine bubble containing ozone is blown into the bottom of the apparatus that is floated. Air bubbles that are floated upwardly are then introduced into a reactor of a tunnel shape and are brought into contact with ultraviolet rays illuminated from the ultraviolet rays lamp built in the reactor.  Due to strong combination of ozone and water. ozone can be sufficiently dissolved in water. The dissolved ozone reacts with UV to maximize the production power of the OH radical.  The generated OH radicals oxidative-decomposed noxious pollutants in water while circulating in the entire water tank.  Installation location: water output unit of the water surface float type in a repository container.  - Function: oxidize non-biodegradable pollutant through formation of OH radicals.  Direct oxidization action due to ozone  Direct photolysis action due to ultraviolet rays  - Mechanism: Ozone of a fine bubble shape reacts with ultraviolet rays illuminated within a tunnel through a photochemical catalysis  - Pollutant to be processed: THM. residual chlorine. volatile pollutant. virus. taste. stink causing materials. and the like.    3. Characteristics  1) Floats on the surface of the water and moves up and down depending on the level of the water.   2) Generate a large amount of OH radicals by allowing ozone fine bubbles to pass through an ultraviolet rays region.    4. Applications  Apartments. school. emergency water supply. public facilities and the like.  Central purification system. food processing factories. factories for processing marine products and so on.": 1,
    "1. Outline  It means the pore control fiber filter. It is made by compressing micro-soft fiber bundles with a rotary unit or compression packs to make pores small. which is then filtered. Afterward. its pores are made large by making it relaxed to back-wash with pressured air or water. It is a new filter that combines the precision filtration function of cartridge and the back-washing function of sandfilter.     2. Introduction(See fig 1. table 1)    3. Characteristics  1) High efficiency and good water quality  - Active sludge-treated water base. efficiency: over 95% and water quality: 5ppm or less  2) Subminiature. light weight and cheap  - volume 1/5 or less. weight (including filter medium) 1/10 or less compared to rapid S.F   3) Long Back-wash time and less back-wash water  - Back-wash time: 2~5 minutes. the quantity of back-wash: around 2~5%  4) Long filter medium life and easy exchange  - pp. Nylon material. Exchange within ten minutes of filter module  5) Automatic product  - When reaching a set pressure. returns to a filtering process after an automatic back-wash    4. Applications  1) Filtering of sewage/foul water/wastewater. and heavy water-treated recycled water  2) Filtering of underground water. purified water tank. drinking water of a spring water company. etc.  3) advanced treatment (activated carbon. the ion top. ozone. UV) and membrane separation (R/O. NF) pre-treatment  4) Filtering for keeping purity in a bathhouse. a swimming pool. a fishing place. an aquarium. etc.  5) Filtering of green/red tide. mud water. etc. in the sea. water-collecting place. a fish-farm. a pond. etc.   6) Filtering of cooling and circulating water in a power plant. an iron plant. etc.. agricultural and industrial water. and the like.": 1,
    "1. Outline  Structure: The air containing dust is introduced into the inside of the housing through the duct by compression or absorption and dusts are attached to the surface of the filtration tube and the filtered clean air pass through the inside of the filtration tube to be discharged through the exit on the top of the tube.    2. Introduction  Structure: vapor is introduced into a housing through a duct by means of sending or inhalation.  Dust is adhered on the surface of the filtration tube.  The filtered clean air passes through the filtration tube and is the exhausted through an upper exit.    Dust adhered on the surface of the filtration tube is automatically consecutively cleaned by a cleaning device of a pulse-jet mode. Dust is collected on a lower hopper and is then exhausted through an exhaust device.  As the filter is not changed in pressure and airflow due to instant cleaning (0.005 ~ 0.1 second). it can consecutively move in a stable state.    The operating principle of the pulsejet mode: Air of a high pressure (5~7kg/cm2) supplied to a compressor is stored in a diaphragm installed at an upper side through an air header. The stored high-pressure air is introduced into a blow tube as a solenoid valve connected thereto is operated.  At this time. the air is sprayed from a nozzle into the filtration tube.    3. Characteristics  1) High dust collection efficiency (99.9%) can be obtained through the use of the felt.  2) As cleaning is instantly performed. width in change of a pressure is small.  A stable consecutive operation is possible.  3) As a good cleaning device and a felt is used. processed airflow per filtering area (1m2) is large and an installation are is small.  4) It can be widely used even in the dust concentration upon to a common environment purification and direct dust collection of an air delivery.   5) Management and maintenance are simple and repair and check are easy in case of a failure.  6) Various types can be applied to wide application depending on usage. purpose. location and installation.    4. Applications  1) Limestone and cement business  2) Wood and paper business  3) Automobile and its related business  4) Smelting furnace and nonferrous metals business  5) Petrochemical industry and carbon business": 1
